      "description": "Watch PSV Eindhoven vs Fortuna Sittard highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 9, 2026. The Eredivisie delivered a high-stakes encounter at the Philips Stadion as PSV Eindhoven hosted Fortuna Sittard . On August 9, 2026 , the crowd witnessed a match of total dominance met by a clinical, never-say-die spirit from the visitors. Dominance Met by a Sudden Setback From the opening whistle, PSV Eindhoven dictated the tempo, commanding an extraordinary 76% of possession. Sven Mijnans was the primary architect in the early stages, delivering several dangerous corners that tested the Fortuna Sittard resolve. However, despite the pressure, it was the visitors who struck first against the run of play. In the 42nd minute, a defensive lapse from Ryan Flamingo gifted an opportunity to Ole Romeny , who clinicaly finished with his right foot to give Fortuna a shock lead heading into the break. Redemption and the PSV Comeback Determined to rectify his earlier error, Ryan Flamingo took matters into his own hands in the second half. In the 55th minute, an inch-perfect corner from Ivan Perisic found the head of Flamingo , who powered the ball home to level the scores. The goal injected fresh energy into the home side, and the pressure on the Fortuna goal became relentless as PSV hunted for a winner. The turnaround was seemingly completed in the 74th minute. Following a key pass from Paul Wanner and an assist by Alassane Plea , Noah Fernandez produced a moment of magic. The forward executed a sublime left-footed lob that left the goalkeeper stranded, putting PSV 2-1 ahead. At that moment, with the hosts in total control, the three points felt secure. Late Drama Silences the Philips Stadion As the match moved into three minutes of added time, Fortuna Sittard mounted one final charge. In the 90+2nd minute, Edouard Michut found space outside the penalty area and unleashed a powerful right-footed strike that flew into the net. The late equalizer stunned the 33,400 fans in attendance. Despite a final corner from Dennis Man in the dying seconds, the match ended in a 2-2 draw, leaving PSV to rue missed opportunities while Fortuna celebrated a hard-earned point."
